From 19e75ab19f960cc52930f14b6da358eee248f0c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:04:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fate/mov: cover complementary st3d and vexu declarations

Generate empty visual sample entries in memory and demux them through
the MOV input format. Compare the observed stereo side data with the
specification's mode table, independently of the parser implementation.

Cover modes 0 through 4, both box orders, inversion and complementary
camera fields, plain and vexu-only entries, reserved modes and duplicate
st3d declarations. No external media sample is needed.

Assisted-by: gpt-6 (Codex)
---
 libavformat/Makefile           |   2 +
 libavformat/tests/mov_stereo.c | 196 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/fate/libavformat.mak     |   4 +
 tests/ref/fate/mov-stereo      |  36 ++++++
 4 files changed, 238 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libavformat/tests/mov_stereo.c
 create mode 100644 tests/ref/fate/mov-stereo

diff --git a/libavformat/Makefile b/libavformat/Makefile
index 92c0971..a582051 100644
--- a/libavformat/Makefile
+++ b/libavformat/Makefile
@@ -814,3 +814,5 @@ TOOLS     = aviocat                                                     \
             seek_print                                                  \
             sidxindex                                                   \
             venc_data_dump
